# UI V2 — v1.3

UI V2 is the incremental replacement for the legacy client interface. v1.3 keeps the unified **Attributes / Skills / Inventory** `CharacterWindow`, the contextual commerce/crafting panel from v1.2, and introduces the first permanent replacement for the classic bottom HUD.

## Layering

```text
Legacy flags / network state
          |
          v
 LegacyUIV2Bridge
       /       \
      v         v
Character UI  PlayerHud
      |         |
      v         v
 ViewModels / semantic gateways
      |
      v
 validated legacy gameplay systems
```

Portable layers (`core`, `input`, `widgets`, `windows`, `pages`, `panels`, `hud`, `domain`, `viewmodels`) do not include `sinLinkHeader.h`, Win32 or DirectX. Legacy state translation stays under `legacy/`; DX9 stays under `rendering/`.

## Character UI

- one movable character shell;
- Attributes / Skills / Inventory tabs;
- real-coordinate pointer input (`pRealCursorPos`);
- actual-window world-input blocking instead of the old `y > 425` rectangle;
- Attributes include the eight resistance channels and per-point stat-impact hints;
- Skills include all legacy skill slots, direct left/right mouse binding and skill-master upgrade;
- Inventory includes Mochila A/B, Armas 1/2, Quest Items, 16 equipment slots, personal-sale markers, lock/costume state and semantic drag/drop adapters.

## Full skill/item details + scrolling

v1.3 restores the large information surfaces that existed in the original client instead of replacing them with short summaries:

- Skills are populated from the legacy `ShowSkillInfo()` document, including description, costs, duration, bonuses and next-level information.
- Items are populated from the legacy `ShowItemInfo()` document, including requirements, stats, aging/mix information and other item-specific properties.
- Long description rows wrap vertically.
- Key/value rows also wrap instead of losing the key to `...`; the value stays right-aligned on the first row.
- Both detail panels support mouse-wheel scrolling and a clickable visual scrollbar.

## Direct skill binding

The extra `Usar esquerda` / `Usar direita` buttons are no longer part of the normal flow:

- left-clicking a learned skill selects it and attempts to bind it to the left mouse side;
- right-clicking selects it and attempts to bind it to the right mouse side;
- the legacy `USECODE` restrictions remain authoritative, so an invalid side is not assigned;
- the normal attack display uses the canonical legacy `NormalAttckName` string to avoid the corrupted slot-name variant.

## Player HUD V2

`PlayerHud` is always available independently of the CharacterWindow and replaces the old bottom chrome with only the requested gameplay essentials:

- HP;
- MP;
- RES/Stamina;
- current left skill;
- current right skill;
- consumables P1 / P2 / P3.

The classic bottom chrome is suppressed while this HUD is active, including the old chat area, X/Q/D/S/V/C buttons, map/camera/run controls, vertical resource bars and old active-skill indicator. Gameplay keyboard shortcuts are not removed by this visual migration.

The V2 potion/consumable slots are interactive through the inventory gateway. The active-skill slots are currently presentation-only; skill selection is done from the Skills tab.

## Font rasterization

The client-wide legacy D3DX font still uses the configured face and the original 16px metrics, but v1.3 requests `ANTIALIASED_QUALITY` instead of `DEFAULT_QUALITY`. This targets the rebuilt/Wine symptom where glyph rows appeared sparse or partially missing. No V2 font family or size override is introduced.

## Contextual commerce/crafting

When a supported context is active, equipment controls on the left side of Inventory are replaced by `ContextPanel`; the bag remains on the right. The panel supports:

- NPC Shop / blacksmith;
- player shop (buyer);
- own Personal Shop (seller/editor);
- Trade;
- Warehouse;
- Mixing / Force;
- Aging;
- Smelting;
- Manufacture;
- Mixture Reset;
- Skin Change;
- Restoration;
- Coin Shop (SCoin);
- Time Coin Shop (TCoin).

Right-clicking a V2 bag item calls `IContextGateway::AcceptInventoryItem(inventoryIndex)`. No modern page passes V2 mouse coordinates into gameplay logic.

The one remaining commerce fallback is the Personal Shop description-entry modal (`MyShopExpBox`), because it is tied directly to the old Win32 IME/edit control.

## Pointer contract

The legacy client remaps `pCursorPos` through `dsMenuCursorPos()` before running the old UI. UI V2 uses `pRealCursorPos`; only compatibility gateways synthesize legacy coordinates inside tightly scoped legacy calls.

## Validation

Run:

```bash
SrcGame/src/systems/ui/v2/tests/run_portable_tests.sh
```

The suite covers runtime lifetime, z-order/input, tabs, attributes, direct skill binding/upgrade, long detail documents, inventory A/B and weapon sets, Quest Items, drag/drop safety, contextual item handoff, Warehouse paging, Coin Shop context, HUD rendering/consumables and dependency boundaries.

The v1.3 portable layer was additionally compiled with `-Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic` and run under AddressSanitizer + UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.

## Remaining work

- V2 text input / IME and Personal Shop description modal;
- potion quantity split dialog;
- keyboard/gamepad focus navigation;
- Quest journal/tracker;
- party/target/minimap redesign;
- optional modern chat replacement (the legacy chat chrome is hidden in v1.3);
- richer HUD interactions/cooldowns and configurable layout.
